<title>BELGIUM: BELGO UNIONS, RENAULT CHIEF MEET IN FRANCE.</title>
<headline>BELGO UNIONS, RENAULT CHIEF MEET IN FRANCE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers and management of Renault's doomed Belgian plant are to meet the French carmaker's Chairman Louis Schweitzer in Beauvais, France, at 1400 GMT on Wednesday, the plant's works council said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The work's council, which includes representatives from unions and management, reiterated in a statement that it disagreed with Renault's shock decision on February 27 to close the Vilvoorde plant in July -- with a loss of 3,100 jobs.</p>
<p>It added it &quot;confirms that all actions will be aimed at keeping the company open&quot;.</p>
<p>It said that closing the Vilvoorde plant or another unit in the group would not solve Renault's problems.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
